{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Crisis at the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Troubleshooting", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Will</span>/<span class=\"italic\">Won't</span> in the <span class=\"italic\">if</span> Clause ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the first conditional to talk about possibilities in the present or future - things which might happen.  You use the <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clause with <span class=\"italic\">Will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Won't</span> to express refusal or disapproval.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"italic\">Will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Won't</span> with an <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clause to focus on the result of the condition rather than a future outcome or possible event. In this case, the use of <span class=\"italic\">will</span> does not refer to the future. <br> <br><span class=\"italic\">Will</span> can be used with an <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clause to suggest disapproval. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If you will keep</span> on being unprofessional, it's no wonder you have so many problems with our customers. = If you insist \u2026</span> <br> <br><span class=\"italic\">Won't</span> can be used with an <span class=\"italic\">if</span> clause to suggest refusal. <br>Example: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If you won't</span> conduct yourself in a professional manner, you'll have to go. = If you refuse ...</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If they won't  be professional, they're done.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If they won't heed my advice, they will be sorry!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you won't conduct yourself in a professional manner, you'll have to go.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Real Conditional: <span class=\"italic\">If </span>and <span class=\"italic\">When </span>to Talk about Real Life Situations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Real Conditional to talk about things you normally do in real-life situations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use both <span class=\"italic\">if</span> and <span class=\"italic\">when</span> in the Present Real Conditional.  <br> <br><span class=\"italic\">If</span> suggests that something happens less frequently.  <br> <br>For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If</span> there are other areas that need improving, I usually like to hear from my staff about it.</span> <br> <br><span class=\"italic\">When</span> suggests that something happens regularly. <br> <br>For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">When</span> I have a day off from work, I <span class=\"strong\">like</span> to go to the mall. </span><br> <br>Notice the structure of this type of conditional: <br> <br><span class=\"italic\">If </span>/ <span class=\"italic\">When </span>... Simple Present ... , ... Simple Present ...", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If it's a reputable brand, it's fine.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It's expensive when you buy a known brand.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When I get feedback, the customers say we need a fresh coat of paint.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make one's blood boil ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to deeply anger ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  When people are late, it makes my blood boil!   ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about customer relations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "What's the damage? ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "what is the cost? ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't worry. What's the damage? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "reputable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a good reputation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  If it's a reputable brand, it's fine.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "troubleshooting ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "discovering why something does not \u200bwork \u200beffectively and making \u200bsuggestions about how to \u200bimprove it ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope I'm doing some troubleshooting here not damage control.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "damage control ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "action taken to limit the damaging effects of an accident or error ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope I'm doing some troubleshooting here and not damage control.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to catch wind of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to hear about  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I caught wind of a story about a waitress undressing in the restaurant?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to undress", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remove clothing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I caught wind of a story about a waitress undressing in the restaurant?  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reprimand ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to officially notify someone that their \u200bbehavior is \u200bwrong and not \u200bacceptable ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If she hasn't been reprimanded, I'll have to insist you do that.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "definitive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "decisive and with authority ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Bill, I've never heard you sound so definitive!  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le01ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to meet expectations ", "type": "name"}, {"co